  "hond": "<div class=\"yomitan-glossary\"><ol data-count=\"1\"><li data-dictionary=\"wty-nl-en\" data-dictionary-id=\"wty-nl-en\" data-has-styles=\"\"><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"partOfSpeech\" title=\"noun\">n</span><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"gender-masculine\" title=\"masculine\">masc</span><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"gender-neuter\" title=\"neuter\">neut</span><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"archaism\" title=\"obsolete\">obs</span><i>(wty-nl-en)</i><ul class=\"gloss-list\" data-count=\"2\"><li class=\"gloss-item\"><div class=\"gloss-content\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"preamble\"><details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-Grammar\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Grammar</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Grammar-content\">hond m (plural honden, diminutive hondje n)</div></details><details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-Etymology\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Etymology</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Etymology-content\">From Middle Dutch hont, from Old Dutch hunt, from Proto-West Germanic *hund, from Proto-Germanic *hundaz, from Proto-Indo-European *ḱwn̥tós, from *ḱwṓ. Cognate to German Hund, English hound.</div></details></div></div><ol class=\"gloss-sc-ol\" data-sc-content=\"glosses\"><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\">dog (Canis lupus familiaris)<details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-examples\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">3 examples</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"extra-info\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"example-sentence\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"example-sentence-a\">De <span class=\"gloss-sc-span\" data-sc-content=\"bold-text\">hond</spa