loss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Grammar</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Grammar-content\">hond n (plural honden, diminutive hondje n)</div></details><details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-Etymology\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Etymology</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Etymology-content\">From Middle Dutch hont, from Old Dutch *hunt, from Proto-Germanic *hundą. Related to honderd.</div></details></div></div><ol class=\"gloss-sc-ol\" data-sc-content=\"glosses\"><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\">an old unit of area measuring 100 roeden, approximately 0.14 hectares</div></li></ol><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"backlink\"><a class=\"gloss-sc-a\" href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hond#Dutch\">Wiktionary</a> | <a class=\"gloss-sc-a\" href=\"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/Dutch/meaning/h/ho/hond.html\">Kaikki</a></div></div></li></ul></li></ol></div>",
  "hart": "<div class=\"yomitan-glossary\"><ol data-count=\"1\"><li data-dictionary=\"wty-nl-en\" data-dictionary-id=\"wty-nl-en\" data-has-styles=\"\"><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"partOfSpeech\" title=\"noun\">n</span><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"gender-feminine\" title=\"feminine\">fem</span><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"gender-neuter\" title=\"neuter\">neut</span><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"\" title=\"non-lemma\">non-lemma</span><i>(wty-nl-en)</i><ul class=\"gloss-list\" data-count=\"2\"><li class=\"gloss-item\"><div class=\"gloss-content\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"preamble\"><details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-Grammar\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Grammar</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Grammar-content\">hart n or f (plural harten, diminutive hartje n)</div></details><details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-Etymology\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Etymology</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Etymology-content\">From Middle Dutch herte, harte, from Old Dutch herta, from Proto-West Germanic *hertā, from Proto-Germanic *hertô, from Proto-Indo-European *ḱḗr.</div></details></div></div><ol class=\"gloss-sc-ol\" data-sc-content=\"glosses\"><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\">heart, main muscle pumping blood through the body</div></li><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\">the center point or zone of an object, image etc.</div></li><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\">the core or essence of some thing, reasoning etc.</div></li><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\">compassionate or similar feelings</div></li></ol><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"backlink\"><a class=\"gloss-sc-a\" href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hart#Dutch\">Wiktionary</a> | <a class=\"gloss-sc-a\" href=\"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/Dutch/meaning/h/ha/hart.html\">Kaikki</a></div></div></li><li class=\"gloss-item\"><div class=\"gloss-content\"><ul class=\"gloss-sc-ul\" style=\"list-style-type: circle\"><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\">hert</li><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\">hert</li><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\">hert</li><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\">hert</li></ul></div></li></ul></li></ol></div>",
  "idee": "<div class=\"yomitan-glossary\"><ol data-count=\"1\"><li data-dictionary=\"wty-nl-en\" data-dictionary-id=\"wty-nl-en\" data-has-styles=\"\"><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"partOfSpeech\" title=\"noun\">n</span><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"gender-feminine\" title=\"feminine\">fem</span><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"gender-neuter\" title=\"neuter\">neut</span><i>(wty-nl-en)</i><ul class=\"gloss-list\" data-count=\"2\"><li class=\"gloss-item\"><div class=\"gloss-content\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"preamble\"><details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-Grammar\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Grammar</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Grammar-content\">idee n (plural ideeën, diminutive ideetje n)</div></details><details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-Etymology\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Etymology</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Etymology-content\">From Middle Dutch idee, borrowed from Middle French idee, from Old French idee, from Latin idea (“a (Platonic) idea; archetype”), from Ancient Greek ἰδέα (idéa, “notion, pattern”), from εἴδω (eídō, “to see”), related to French idée.</div></details></div></div><ol class=\"gloss-sc-ol\" data-sc-content=\"glosses\"><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\">idea<details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-examples\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">1 example</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"extra-info\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"example-sentence\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"example-sentence-a\">Het <span class=\"gloss-sc-span\" data-sc-content=\"bold-text\">idee</span> om een datacentrum te bouwen dichtbij het dorp stuitte op weerstand.</div><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"example-sentence-b\">The <span class=\"gloss-sc-span\" data-sc-content=\"bold-text\">idea</span> to build a data centre near the village met with opposition.</div></div></div></details></div></li></ol><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"backlink\"><a class=\"gloss-sc-a\" href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idee#Dutch\">Wiktionary</a> | <a class=\"gloss-sc-a\" href=\"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/Dutch/meaning/i/id/idee.html\">Kaikki</a></div></div></li><li class=\"gloss-item\"><div class=\"gloss-content\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"preamble\"><details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-Grammar\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Grammar</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Grammar-content\">idee n or f (plural ideeën)</div></details><details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-Etymology\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Etymology</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Etymology-content\">From Middle Dutch idee, borrowed from Middle French idee, from Old French idee, from Latin idea (“a (Platonic) idea; archetype”), from Ancient Greek ἰδέα (idéa, “notion, pattern”), from εἴδω (eídō, “to see”), related to French idée.</div></details></div></div><ol class=\"gloss-sc-ol\" data-sc-content=\"glosses\"><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"tags\"><span class=\"gloss-sc-span\" data-sc-content=\"tag\" data-sc-category=\"topic\" title=\"philosophy\">philos</span></div>idea, notion<details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-examples\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">1 example</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"extra-info\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"example-sentence\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"example-sentence-a\">De <span class=\"gloss-sc-span\" data-sc-content=\"bold-text\">idee</span> van een universele moraliteit is wijdverspreid.</div><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"example-sentence-b\">The <span class=\"gloss-sc-span\" data-sc-content=\"bold-text\">notion</span> of a universal morality is widespread.</div></div></div></details></div></li></ol><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"backlink\"><a class=\"gloss-sc-a\" href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idee#Dutch\">Wiktionary</a> | <a class=\"gloss-sc-a\" href=\"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/Dutch/meaning/i/id/idee.html\">Kaikki</a></div></div></li></ul></li></ol></div>",
  "e-mail": "<div class=\"yomitan-glossary\"><ol data-count=\"1\"><li data-dictionary=\"wty-nl-en\" data-dictionary-id=\"wty-nl-en\" data-has-styles=\"\"><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"partOfSpeech\" title=\"noun\">n</span><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"gender-masculine\" title=\"masculine\">masc</span><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"\" title=\"non-lemma\">non-lemma</span><i>(wty-nl-en)</i><ul class=\"gloss-list\" data-count=\"2\"><li class=\"gloss-item\"><div class=\"gloss-content\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"preamble\"><details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-Grammar\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Grammar</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Grammar-content\">e-mail m (plural e-mails, diminutive e-mailtje n)</div></details><details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-Etymology\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Etymology</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Etymology-content\">Borrowed from English e-mail.</div></details></div></div><ol class=\"gloss-sc-ol\" data-sc-content=\"glosses\"><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\">e-mail</div></li></ol><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"backlink\"><a class=\"gloss-sc-a\" href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/e-mail#Dutch\">Wiktionary</a> | <a class=\"gloss-sc-a\" href=\"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/Dutch/meaning/e/e-/e-mail.html\">Kaikki</a></div></div></li><li class=\"gloss-item\"><div class=\"gloss-content\"><ul class=\"gloss-sc-ul\" style=\"list-style-type: circle\"><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\">e-mailen</li><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\">e-mailen</li></ul></div></li></ul></li></ol></div>",
  "student": "<div class=\"yomitan-glossary\"><ol data-count=\"1\"><li data-dictionary=\"wty-nl-en\" data-dictionary-id=\"wty-nl-en\" data-has-styles=\"\"><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"partOfSpeech\" title=\"noun\">n</span><span class=\"gloss-tag\" data-category=\"gender-masculine\" title=\"masculine\">masc</span><i>(wty-nl-en)</i><ul class=\"gloss-list\" data-count=\"1\"><li class=\"gloss-item\"><div class=\"gloss-content\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"preamble\"><details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-Grammar\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Grammar</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Grammar-content\">student m (plural studenten, diminutive studentje n, feminine studente)</div></details><details class=\"gloss-sc-details\" data-sc-content=\"details-entry-Etymology\"><summary class=\"gloss-sc-summary\" data-sc-content=\"summary-entry\">Etymology</summary><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"Etymology-content\">Borrowed from Latin studēns, present participle of studēre (“to study”).</div></details></div></div><ol class=\"gloss-sc-ol\" data-sc-content=\"glosses\"><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\">a student at an institute for academic tertiary education</div></li><li class=\"gloss-sc-li\"><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\">a student at an institute for secondary or tertiary education.</div></li></ol><div class=\"gloss-sc-div\" data-sc-content=\"backlink\"><a class=\"gloss-sc-a\" href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/student#Dutch\">Wiktionary</a> | <a class=\"gloss-sc-a\" href=\"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/Dutch/meaning/s/st/student.html\">Kaikki</a></div></div></li></ul></li></ol></div>"
